File: websocket-server.ts
Purpose: Central WebSocket manager for the positioning server. Handles UWB device connections, message routing, position broadcasting, and live log event delivery to dashboard clients.

Recent Changes:
- Added dashboardClients: Set<WebSocket> to track browser dashboard connections separately from UWB devices
- Added broadcastLog(level, event, detail?) public method: sends log_event messages to all open dashboard sockets
- handleRegister: detects dashboard registration (device_type/deviceType === 'dashboard'), adds ws to dashboardClients, skips UWB device flow
- handleDisconnect: checks dashboardClients first and removes ws; skips device teardown for dashboard sockets
- Added broadcastLog calls at: device registration, device disconnect, ranging report received, position computed, heartbeat received

Key Components:
- broadcastLog(): Constructs LogEventMessage (ISO timestamp, level, event, optional detail) and sends to all dashboard clients
- handleRegister(): Now bifurcates between dashboard clients and UWB devices via duck-typed check on device_type/deviceType
- handleRanging(): Emits two log events - one for ranging measurement, one when position is computed
- handleDisconnect(): Emits warn-level log event with device id before removing from maps

Dependencies:
- ../config/types: LogEventMessage, LogEventLevel (newly added types)
- ../positioning/multilateration: positionEngine.computePosition()
- ../positioning/ranging-buffer: rangingBuffer.addMeasurement()
- ../config/anchor-config: anchorConfig.getAnchorList()

Architecture Notes:
- Dashboard clients are identified by a camelCase or snake_case device_type of 'dashboard' (sent by the frontend on ws.onopen)
- dashboardClients set is separate from devices map; dashboard sockets never enter wsToDevice or devices maps
- broadcastLog is public so it can be called from other server modules in future
- Log events are push-only from server to dashboard; no client-side log messages are expected
